## 3. Permitted Purposes

Any purpose is a permitted purpose for:

(a) an individual using the software for themselves; and

(b) an organization in which no more than three (3) individuals use the
software, counting the organization together with all of its affiliates.

Any other use, including use within an organization in which more than three
(3) individuals use the software, is not a permitted purpose. That use needs a
separate commercial license from the licensor, which you can ask for through
the contact form at https://pierre-review.com/contact.

## 4. No Competing Use

No purpose is a permitted purpose if it is a competing use. A competing use is
making the software, or any product or service substantially similar to it or
built from it, available to others as a commercial product or service, whether
as installable software, a hosted service or any other form.

## 5. Distribution License

The licensor grants you an additional copyright license to distribute copies of
the software. Your license to distribute covers distributing the software with
changes and new works permitted by section 6 (Changes and New Works License).

## 6. Changes and New Works License

The licensor grants you an additional copyright license to make changes and new
works based on the software for any permitted purpose.

## 7. Notices

You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any part of the software from
you also gets a copy of these terms, together with the copyright notice above.
Anyone who gets a copy from you gets it under these terms only, and no other
terms. If you modify the software, you must include in any modified copies of
