## 14. Definitions

The **licensor** is Alex Wakeman, the individual offering these terms, and the
**software** is the software the licensor makes available under these terms,
including any version of it.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these terms.

**Your company** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship, or other kind of
organization that you work for, plus all organizations that have control over,
are under the control of, or are under common control with that organization.

An **organization** includes any company, firm, partnership, government body,
charity, team or other group of people working together, and **affiliates** of
an organization are all organizations that have control over, are under the
control of, or are under common control with it. **Control** means ownership of
substantially all the assets of an entity, or the power to direct its
management and policies by vote, contract, or otherwise. Control can be direct
or indirect.

An individual **uses** the software within an organization if they run it, or
work with it directly, in the course of their work for, or on behalf of, that
organization.

**Your licenses** are all the licenses granted to you for the software under
these terms.

**Use** means anything you do with the software requiring one of your licenses.
